            <ArticleTitle>[Percutaneous thermocoagulation of sensory lumbar nerve roots in the treatment of pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study was carried out on the experiences with 20 patients with low back pain. They were treated by thermoelectrocoagulation of the posterior lumbar roots. 60% optimal and 10% good results without permanent complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
